{location:p.e4,reason:"E004 stipulates unnormalized norms for the same spatial product."}],
justification:"The change of spatial measure multiplies the squared L2-based weighted Fourier norm by 2*pi, so the norm scales by its square root, at negative as well as positive Sobolev orders. Essential suprema and addition of norm components preserve this fixed scaling. Thus cubic estimates acquire factor 2*pi and quadratic estimates factor sqrt(2*pi), absorbed into constants."
