grounds:[{location:"/definitions/3",reason:"S_t has multiplier exp(i*t*k^3)."},
{location:"/definitions/2",reason:"H^r is the weighted Fourier-square space."},
{location:"/definitions/8",reason:"B_t is the conjugated spatial derivative of the product."},
{location:"/definitions/11",reason:"Stage on smooth inputs is one half the time integral of B."},
{location:p.s2,reason:"The stage data have a>=0 and tau>0."}],
justification:"Multiplication of the Fourier phases adds their time parameters; their modulus is one, their zero-frequency value is one, and the phases at opposite frequencies are conjugates. These facts prove the group, norm and symmetry assertions. Substituting the group law into B gives B_(a+r)(w,w)=S_(-a)B_r(S_a w,S_a w); changing the smooth integral variable to r yields the Stage identity. This establishes the identity independently of any source estimate or source-grid identification."
